## Fixed automation contract

- Keep exactly one active Ops Brief automation: `2:45 AM/PM Eastern Ops Brief`; exact `RRULE:FREQ=DAILY;BYHOUR=2,14;BYMINUTE=45;BYSECOND=0`, timezone `America/New_York`. It invokes the skill, selects AM/PM from local time, treats PM as morning, and returns only the brief.
- Keep exactly one active `Receipt & Order Lifecycle`: exact 1:45 AM/PM Eastern, `RRULE:FREQ=DAILY;BYHOUR=1,13;BYMINUTE=45`, `timing_mode=exact_schedule`.
- Never create per-order jobs/events or revive 3:00, Pacific, UTC-shifted, duplicate, child, support, or retry jobs. Scheduled runs never inspect or mutate automations.

## Invariants

- A clear Ops-list change from any supported conversation is an immediate canonical Sheet write; preserve history with `Done` or `Removed`.
- Briefs use live evidence/engine output. Read complete Gmail evidence; reconcile `Shipments`; remove delivered items, retain `Order Events`, and report once.
- Important actionable mail stays under `Ops/Archive Approval` until explicit approval. Never send email automatically or delete Gmail without an explicit bounded request.
- HOME/ROAD uses live controls/trips. A clear Home early closes current mileage accrual and holds HOME through the next Friday 2:45 PM brief. Terminal paid miles are directional; never mirror an unevidenced reverse value.
- One purchase has one Receipt ID/total and may contain line items in different categories/assets/projects. Classify items independently, verify identifiable part/SKU fitment from credible evidence, and keep balanced allocations so spend is counted once.
- Preserve cancelled/returned history. Cancellation and refund are separate facts; verify expected money resolution from merchant/account evidence and surface unresolved corrections after five business days.
- Unknown classification/fitment stays queued; never guess. Gmail archival/success requires the Audit gate to pass database, Drive, classification, allocation, mapping, Shipment, financial-resolution, and required inventory checks.

